{
 "name": "call_frames_v1",
 "spec": "CIRISServer 0.5.246 call frames socket, WS /v1/chat/{room}/call/frames; one WebSocket binary message = one frame; integers big-endian. Agreed with CIRISClient CSD-134 (PR #287) and CIRISEdge.",
 "layout": {
  "client_to_node": "ver u8 (=1) | codec_id u8 | spatial u8 | temporal u8 | quality u8 | payload...",
  "node_to_client": "ver u8 (=1) | codec_id u8 | spatial u8 | temporal u8 | quality u8 | pub_len u16 | publisher[pub_len] UTF-8 key_id | stream_id[32] | epoch u64 | chunk_seq u64 | payload..."
 },
 "audio_payload": "opus/48000/1/20ms",
 "notes": [
  "Audio: codec_id 0xFF (edge CODEC_OPAQUE), layer (0,0,0), payload = exactly one Opus packet (RFC 6716), 48 kHz mono, 20 ms, VBR, VOIP application, 24-32 kbit/s. No inner header; no DTX or FEC in v1; the app does PLC.",
  "Video: codec_id is passed through unchanged. Which video codec is open (edge registers only 0x01 AV1 SVC; 0x02/0x03 reserved) and pending Eric and the CC; frames v1 pins no video rule.",
  "codec_id 0xFF with a layer other than (0,0,0) is refused (edge requires the base cell for opaque chunks).",
  "publisher is at most 256 bytes. A payload over the call's frame_budget_bytes is refused with a text event, never cut; that check is the route's, not the codec's.",
  "The opus vector payload is a real 60-byte packet: TOC 0x78 (hybrid full-band, mono, one 20 ms frame), a 440 Hz tone encoded by libopus."
 ],
